  "facts": [
    "Opened in 1992 as part of the Rennesøy Fixed Link, the Byfjord Tunnel was Europe's longest and deepest sub‑sea road tunnel at the time, stretching 5,875 metres beneath the Byfjorden.",
    "With a maximum 8% grade, the tunnel plunges 223 metres below sea level, making it the deepest point of any Norwegian road tunnel when it first opened.",
    "Until 2006, the Byfjord Tunnel operated as a toll road, collecting fees from an average daily traffic of 9,717 vehicles in 2018."
